{"type": "stdout", "ts": 12500, "data": "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-7\",\"id\":\"msg_01EQ71aNky2fL4UxL8cBx6y6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# Working through the problem\\n\\n**Starting apples:** 47\\n\\n**Step 1 \u2014 Sell 3/7:**\\n3/7 \u00d7 47 = 141/7 \u2248 20.14 apples\\n\\nNote: 47 isn't divisible by 7, so this yields a non-integer. I'll carry the exact fraction.\\n\\nRevenue: (141/7) \u00d7 $2.25 = $317.25 / 7 \u2248 **$45.32**\\nRemaining: 47 \u2212 141/7 = 188/7 \u2248 26.86 apples\\n\\n**Step 2 \u2014 Buy 12 more:**\\nInventory: 188/7 + 12 = 272/7 \u2248 38.86 apples\\nAdded cost: 12 \u00d7 $1.50 = **$18.00**\\n\\n**Step 3 \u2014 Give away 1/4:**\\nGiven away: 1/4 \u00d7 272/7 = 68/7 \u2248 9.71 apples (no revenue)\\nRemaining: 204/7 \u2248 29.14 apples (unsold inventory)\\n\\n# Profit calculation\\n\\nAssuming the original 47 were also bought at wholesale:\\n\\n- **Total cost:** (47 \u00d7 $1.50) + $18.00 = $70.50 + $18.00 = **$88.50**\\n- **Total revenue:** \u2248 **$45.32**\\n- **Profit:** $45.32 \u2212 $88.50 \u2248 **\u2212$43.18 (a loss)**\\n\\nIf instead you only count cost-of-goods-sold (the 141/7 apples actually sold at wholesale $1.50):\\n- COGS: (141/7) \u00d7 $1.50 \u2248 $30.21\\n- Profit on sold apples: $45.32 \u2212 $30.21 \u2248 **$15.11**\\n- But he also spent $18 on 12 apples he didn't sell, so net cash \u2248 **\u2212$2.89**\\n\\n**Answer depends on accounting choice**, but the straightforward reading (all apples cost $1.50 wholesale) gives a **loss of ~$43.18**. The problem is also slightly ill-posed since 3/7 of 47 isn't a whole apple.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":6,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":27325,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":27325},\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"d1e38369-d212-4307-b8ff-ff734596e0c3\",\"uuid\":\"6323461b-7a08-4ea9-b11d-769fb54d1962\"}"}
{"type": "stdout", "ts": 13000, "data": "{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":16366,\"duration_api_ms\":17827,\"num_turns\":1,\"result\":\"# Working through the problem\\n\\n**Starting apples:** 47\\n\\n**Step 1 \u2014 Sell 3/7:**\\n3/7 \u00d7 47 = 141/7 \u2248 20.14 apples\\n\\nNote: 47 isn't divisible by 7, so this yields a non-integer. I'll carry the exact fraction.\\n\\nRevenue: (141/7) \u00d7 $2.25 = $317.25 / 7 \u2248 **$45.32**\\nRemaining: 47 \u2212 141/7 = 188/7 \u2248 26.86 apples\\n\\n**Step 2 \u2014 Buy 12 more:**\\nInventory: 188/7 + 12 = 272/7 \u2248 38.86 apples\\nAdded cost: 12 \u00d7 $1.50 = **$18.00**\\n\\n**Step 3 \u2014 Give away 1/4:**\\nGiven away: 1/4 \u00d7 272/7 = 68/7 \u2248 9.71 apples (no revenue)\\nRemaining: 204/7 \u2248 29.14 apples (unsold inventory)\\n\\n# Profit calculation\\n\\nAssuming the original 47 were also bought at wholesale:\\n\\n- **Total cost:** (47 \u00d7 $1.50) + $18.00 = $70.50 + $18.00 = **$88.50**\\n- **Total revenue:** \u2248 **$45.32**\\n- **Profit:** $45.32 \u2212 $88.50 \u2248 **\u2212$43.18 (a loss)**\\n\\nIf instead you only count cost-of-goods-sold (the 141/7 apples actually sold at wholesale $1.50):\\n- COGS: (141/7) \u00d7 $1.50 \u2248 $30.21\\n- Profit on sold apples: $45.32 \u2212 $30.21 \u2248 **$15.11**\\n- But he also spent $18 on 12 apples he didn't sell, so net cash \u2248 **\u2212$2.89**\\n\\n**Answer depends on accounting choice**, but the straightforward reading (all apples cost $1.50 wholesale) gives a **loss of ~$43.18**. The problem is also slightly ill-posed since 3/7 of 47 isn't a whole apple.\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"d1e38369-d212-4307-b8ff-ff734596e0c3\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.20212524999999998,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":6,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":27325,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1234,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\